  "body": "Found by the QA runs of 2026-11-18 (CamCraft main `83867fd7`), parts p02 (bracket) and p03 (stepped block), independently.\n\nWhat happens: a 2D Contour with tabs and `tab_height` set (for example 1.5 mm) leaves tabs as tall as one stepdown (about 4 mm with a 4 mm stepdown): the tabs start at the next stepdown level, not at `tab_height` above the bottom. No note says the height was changed.\n\nWhy it matters: the tabs are about 4x stronger than asked; they are hard to break off and need much more clean-up. The part stays held, so it is not unsafe, but the result is not what the user set.\n\nRelated, not the same: #2562 (a band boundary inside the tab height makes the tab shorter), #2480 (tab width minus the tool diameter).\n\nDone means: the tab's top is at bottom + `tab_height` for any stepdown (a pass at exactly that level when needed), pinned by a test that measures the tab height for stepdowns larger and smaller than `tab_height`; or, if a level must be skipped, a note that names the real height.\n",
